think Read the road: REMEMBER inner loop, the 1024-round itinerary, the eight-season double-seat, the Rye-first crypto-parity wave. Live edge is Season G open-media; the last laps grew image/text_grid.rye a per-cell FOREGROUND palette (render_grid_fg) and scooter_paint painted a live conversation to pixels in color.
think Lindy-first crux-first: the colored terminal had per-cell fg over ONE shared bg. A real terminal cell carries an ink AND a ground -- that is what makes a header bar, a selected row, an unread badge. The smallest tractable move that completes the colored-terminal cell model is a per-cell BACKGROUND. Floor code, does not wait on paused Brushstroke.
think Rota lap read item 22 (context/SILO_TECHNIQUE.md) -- understand, abstract, re-express in our own voice; the colored-terminal idea enters owned, no borrowed dress.
think Design: fill_cell writes a cell's whole col_pitch x cell_h block bg DIRECTLY (a straight set), so a grid whose every cell shares one ground reproduces solid(bg) byte-for-byte -- the parity the colored verb rests on. paint_grid_cells fills each cell's ground then paints its glyph in its own fg over it (a real terminal cell). render_grid_cells sizes the image exactly; the cells tile it, so no base fill shows through.
obs Witness-first, red-then-green in the same round: uniform-ground render equals render_grid_fg pixel-for-pixel (tiling parity); a blue header bar leaves no band pixel white and shows pure blue between the glyphs; changed pixels >= the whole blue band; the colored terminal round-trips through QOI byte-for-byte; a wrong-length bg refuses GridBgMismatch by name before a pixel is allocated.
obs Bounds: every buffer names a max (grid_cols_max, grid_rows_max, qoi's pixel ceiling), the box is checked all-or-nothing once up front, u32 counts and u8 color bytes, >=2 asserts per fn. No network, no key, no funds.
loom witness=text_grid_witness grid=16x3 image_px=96x21 ink_px=291 result=GREEN
